{
  "comment": [
    "Word lists for the prose checker. Kept as a resource rather than in the",
    "source so the lists can be edited, extended or translated without a",
    "rebuild: Resources/Data is a folder reference, so this file ships as it",
    "is found here.",
    "",
    "English and Italian entries share the categories rather than living in",
    "separate ones, so a document in either language — or one that mixes",
    "them — is checked without anything having to know which it is.",
    "",
    "Each category needs an id, a name, a colour and at least one of words or",
    "phrases. words match whole words only; phrases match a run of words with",
    "any whitespace between them. Matching is case insensitive throughout.",
    "",
    "Write entries without trailing punctuation: the patterns are wrapped in",
    "word boundaries, and an entry ending in an apostrophe can never match.",
    "\"un po\" is the way to catch \"un po'\".",
    "",
    "repeated.exceptions lists doublings that are meant: Italian is full of",
    "them — piano piano, via via, man mano — and flagging those would make",
    "the whole category untrustworthy.",
    "",
    "Colours are used for the underline drawn under a flagged word, so they",
    "need to stay legible over both a light and a dark editor theme. The",
    "Solarized accent colours below hold up on both."
  ],
